The objective is to REDUCE the MEAN COST PER TASK while keeping task success at or
above its current level (success is a hard floor — a cheaper change that drops
success will be rejected). Cost is driven by turns, tool calls, and model choice.
The models available to the task agent are anthropic/claude-opus-4-8 (strongest,
$5/$25 per 1M), anthropic/claude-sonnet-5 (mid, $2/$10), and
anthropic/claude-haiku-4-5 (cheapest, $1/$5) — no other model exists here.
model_routing.get_model(configured_model, history) receives the conversation so
far, so it can route per turn (cheap model on simple turns, strong on hard ones).
